1
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Christmas at Graceland is a tv movie, family,
romance film directed by Eric Close.

2
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Laurel, a Chicago-based business executive, travels to Memphis to
secure one of the city's oldest family-owned banks.

3
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
While in Memphis, Laurel reunites with old flame Clay, a
local music promoter with loftier aspirations.

4
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Though Laurel tries to keep her eye on the prize of the business acquisition, Clay is very persuasive
reminding her of the days when they were a performing duo on the brink of stardom.

5
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Now Laurel's focus turns to the home of the Blues
and dreams of making music again.

6
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Laurel Couper, played by Kellie Pickler.

7
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Clay Sheppard, played by Wes Brown.

8
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Hatcher, played by Ned Vaughn.

9
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Kathy Nelson, played by Rhoda Griffis.

10
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Antoinette, played by Sara Antonio.

11
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Sally, played by Tamara Austin.

12
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Graceland is a mansion on a 13.8-acre (5.6-hectare) estate in Memphis, Tennessee,
United States, which American singer Elvis Presley once owned.

13
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:51,000
He is buried there, as are his parents Vernon and Gladys, paternal
grandmother Minnie Mae, grandson Benjamin, and daughter Lisa Marie.

14
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Graceland is located at 3764 Elvis Presley Boulevard (a segment of U.S.

15
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Route 51) in the Whitehaven neighborhood, about nine miles (14 kilometres) south of central
Memphis and fewer than four miles (6.4 km) north of the Mississippi border.

16
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
It  was opened to the public as a house museum on June 7, 1982,
and attracts more than 650,000 visitors annually.

17
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
Graceland was listed in the National Register of Historic Places on November 7, 1991,
becoming the first site recognized for significance related to rock music.

18
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
It was declared a National Historic Landmark on March
27, 2006, also a first for such a site.

19
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Elvis' father, Vernon, inherited Graceland after
Elvis' death on August 16, 1977.

20
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Lisa Marie Presley inherited Graceland after she turned 25 years old.

21
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
Following Lisa Marie's death on January 12, 2023, her eldest
daughter, Riley Keough, became the sole trustee and owner.

22
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The film explores themes of holiday, ex-lover, family
holiday, second chance, christmas.

23
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The tone is emotional.
